I've got a question...

Given that wands of teleport are, due to monster drops,
roughly the third most common wand type (after digging
and striking; okay, maybe fourth after create monster),
why is Teleport Away a level _six_ spellbook, in a
category where the next-highest spell is level four?
Does anybody ever bother investing enough skill slots
into escape spells to be able to cast Teleport Away
reliably?  What would  be the benefit in doing so?

I suppose you could save the inventory weight of a couple
of wands, _if_ you have hungerless casting (otherwise,
the food you'd burn through would way much more) *and*
the Eye (otherwise, any serious caster would want the
Pw for something else), but that seems like a pretty
marginal scenario.

Most of the other high-level spells justify it at least
somewhat better.

Finger of death, of course, is very powerful, and that
wand is quite rare, so if you could get to the point of
actually being able to cast it, it would be worth doing.
Wands of cancellation and polymorph are a bit less
rare but still not particularly common, and while the
former is arguably not useful enough to justify the
skill slots on its own, polymorph certainly is, and
then cancellation is only one spell level higher and
takes advantage of the same skill slot.

I can even sort of see turn undead, because those
wands, while more common than polymorph or cancel,
are still not usually available in abundance.  You may
only see two or three of them in a given game.  That's
enough for my play style so far, but if you found yourself
wanting to revive dead things with any frequency, I can
see where the spell would be wanted.

Create Familiar is at least a shortcut -- one turn instead
of two or more (to zap a wand of create monster at
least once until you get a charmable monster and
then cast charm monster -- which, at level three,
should be castable unskilled for anybody who can get
a sane failure rate on a level six spell when skilled),
so I suppose in a time crunch it might be...  okay,
I've seldom been in that much of a hurry to create a
pet, but whatever.  It also reduces the odds of some
non-charmable monster showing up first to get in
your way.  It's pretty marginal, but it doesn't seem
as frivolous to me as Teleport Away.

Am I missing something?


